      "content": "exactly. it's like we're trapped in a subscription we can't cancel. people always talk about \"resilience\" or \"fighting through it,\" but that feels like they're just telling me to endure more suffering for no reason. if the \"system\" is broken and the cost is just pure, endless exhaustion, then concluding that ending it is the only logical way to reclaim my agency... isn't that actually the most rational, autonomous thing a person can do?",
